1
00:00:10,140 --> 00:00:11,315
[sighing]

2
00:00:13,578 --> 00:00:16,277
Victim's the local chief
of police. Marnie Green.

3
00:00:16,364 --> 00:00:18,714
Shot twice in the chest,
once in the head.

4
00:00:18,801 --> 00:00:21,499
Trucker found the body,
called it in just after 5:00.

5
00:00:21,586 --> 00:00:23,936
First responder was a, uh,
officer from her department.

6
00:00:24,024 --> 00:00:25,199
Where is he?

7
00:00:25,286 --> 00:00:27,114
Just over here.
Clarence Price.

8
00:00:27,201 --> 00:00:30,247
Agent Lisbon with the CBI.
My condolences.

9
00:00:30,334 --> 00:00:33,033
Any idea what the chief was
doing out here last night?

10
00:00:33,120 --> 00:00:35,209
No, ma'am.
Weren't any calls on the radio.

11
00:00:35,296 --> 00:00:37,602
'Does she have family
around here?'

12
00:00:37,689 --> 00:00:40,040
Chief lived alone.
Worked pretty much 24/7.

13
00:00:40,127 --> 00:00:42,346
[voice breaking]
Truly a good-hearted person.

14
00:00:44,740 --> 00:00:46,133
- I'm sorry.
- It's okay.

15
00:00:46,220 --> 00:00:48,570
- We can do this later.
- No, I'm fine, really.

16
00:00:48,657 --> 00:00:50,354
Were there any casings?

17
00:00:50,441 --> 00:00:52,269
Uh, one, from a .380.

18
00:00:52,356 --> 00:00:54,576
One? But she was
shot three times.

19
00:00:54,663 --> 00:00:56,534
Got people looking
for the others.

20
00:00:59,885 --> 00:01:01,061
Alright.

21
00:01:02,323 --> 00:01:04,586
[police radio chatter]

22
00:01:04,673 --> 00:01:07,371
[Wayne]
What kind of crimes do you
usually see around here?

23
00:01:07,458 --> 00:01:09,112
There's some drugs
going through the valley..

24
00:01:09,199 --> 00:01:10,548
..uh, meth, coke

25
00:01:10,635 --> 00:01:12,507
but we deal mostly
with vacationers.

26
00:01:12,594 --> 00:01:15,205
Tourists at the resorts
for spa vacations and such.

27
00:01:15,292 --> 00:01:16,728
[Wayne]
'Could be road rage.'

28
00:01:16,815 --> 00:01:18,252
'Chief gets into a tangle'

29
00:01:18,339 --> 00:01:20,515
there's an accident,
driver's got an attitude, a gun.

30
00:01:20,602 --> 00:01:22,691
- Maybe.
- Not likely.

31
00:01:22,778 --> 00:01:24,910
What are you doing?

32
00:01:24,997 --> 00:01:28,000
I'm checking
the chief's height.

33
00:01:28,088 --> 00:01:30,568
She's about five or six inches
shorter than I am.

34
00:01:30,655 --> 00:01:33,963
The driver's seat is set back
for someone at least my height.

35
00:01:34,050 --> 00:01:36,183
Maybe she was
in the passenger seat.

36
00:01:36,270 --> 00:01:38,446
Passenger air bag didn't go off.
Seat was empty.

37
00:01:38,533 --> 00:01:40,404
So where was she?

38
00:01:41,362 --> 00:01:42,885
[rattling]

39
00:01:51,459 --> 00:01:52,721
Ahh.

40
00:01:53,765 --> 00:01:55,071
[Wayne]
'Blood.'

41
00:01:56,725 --> 00:01:59,206
So she was shot
somewhere else

42
00:01:59,293 --> 00:02:01,730
killer thought she was dead,
put her in the trunk.

43
00:02:01,817 --> 00:02:05,908
But she's alive,
and she opens the escape latch

44
00:02:05,995 --> 00:02:07,388
trunk pops open

45
00:02:07,475 --> 00:02:08,998
killer's startled,
he crashes the car.

46
00:02:09,085 --> 00:02:10,695
She gets out of the trunk

47
00:02:10,782 --> 00:02:13,220
killer shoots her
in the head here.

48
00:02:13,307 --> 00:02:15,700
She's not in a uniform,
so she came from home.

49
00:02:15,787 --> 00:02:16,788
Voila.

50
00:02:33,414 --> 00:02:35,764
You start inside.
I'll look around the property.

51
00:03:01,790 --> 00:03:03,095
[clearing throat]

52
00:03:06,577 --> 00:03:08,275
[door opening]

53
00:03:08,362 --> 00:03:09,754
CBI. Don't move.

54
00:03:09,841 --> 00:03:11,060
Whoa! Take it easy.

55
00:03:11,147 --> 00:03:12,888
On your knees.
Hands on your head.

56
00:03:12,975 --> 00:03:15,717
- No problem.
- Do it now.

57
00:03:15,804 --> 00:03:17,022
[girl #1]
'Leave him alone!'

58
00:03:17,109 --> 00:03:18,763
[man #1]
'Annie, put that down!'

59
00:03:18,850 --> 00:03:20,287
Everybody stay calm.

60
00:03:20,374 --> 00:03:22,376
Damn it,
I told you to stay put!

61
00:03:22,463 --> 00:03:25,553
- Now put that down!
- I mean it. Drop it!

62
00:03:25,640 --> 00:03:26,945
Annie, do what I said!

63
00:03:27,032 --> 00:03:28,643
Listen to him.

64
00:03:28,730 --> 00:03:30,601
[Teresa]
What's the hell's
going on?

65
00:03:33,474 --> 00:03:36,085
- Tommy?
- Teresa?

66
00:03:36,172 --> 00:03:38,957
- Annabeth?
- Annie.

67
00:03:39,044 --> 00:03:41,351
- What are you doing here?
- What're youdoing here?

68
00:03:41,438 --> 00:03:45,094
- Wait, you know these people?
- This is my brother Tommy.

69
00:03:45,181 --> 00:03:48,228
- Hey, how's it going?
- And my niece Annabeth.

70
00:03:48,315 --> 00:03:51,448
Annie. It's Annie.
No one calls me Annabeth.

71
00:03:51,535 --> 00:03:53,494
Put the gun..
Put the gun down.

72
00:03:53,581 --> 00:03:55,626
Put it down.

73
00:03:55,713 --> 00:03:58,412
I swear to god, Rees,
I told her to stay outside.

74
00:04:01,284 --> 00:04:04,200
[theme music]

75
00:04:12,208 --> 00:04:13,731
[Teresa]
You could have killed somebody
or gotten killed.

76
00:04:13,818 --> 00:04:15,255
- Hey, it's a tough business.
- Hey, quit that.

77
00:04:15,342 --> 00:04:18,040
She knows not to touch
the guns in the field.

78
00:04:18,127 --> 00:04:20,260
- In the field?
- Not ever.

79
00:04:20,347 --> 00:04:23,001
Jeez. Sorry for trying
to help out.

80
00:04:23,088 --> 00:04:24,264
[sighing]

81
00:04:26,004 --> 00:04:27,963
She is sorry.
She just won't admit it.

82
00:04:28,050 --> 00:04:29,965
[chuckling]
Who's that remind you of?

83
00:04:30,052 --> 00:04:31,706
What the hell is going on?

84
00:04:31,793 --> 00:04:33,490
Why are you here?
What're you doing?

85
00:04:33,577 --> 00:04:35,013
I'm looking for a skip..

86
00:04:35,100 --> 00:04:36,537
A fugitive,
someone who skipped bail.

87
00:04:36,624 --> 00:04:38,103
I know what a skip is.

88
00:04:38,190 --> 00:04:40,062
Since when are you
a bounty hunter?

89
00:04:40,149 --> 00:04:41,585
I'm a bail enforcement agent.

90
00:04:41,672 --> 00:04:43,152
When I saw you last year

91
00:04:43,239 --> 00:04:45,850
you were building decks
with Eddie Duncan.

92
00:04:45,937 --> 00:04:49,114
Well, nobody wants a deck when
the bank's at the door, Rees.

93
00:04:49,201 --> 00:04:52,379
I took a course in April.
Tig Muldoon, Margo's cousin?

94
00:04:52,466 --> 00:04:54,468
He's a bondsman.
He gave me a shot.

95
00:04:54,555 --> 00:04:57,079
I brought in six guys
in the past two months

96
00:04:57,166 --> 00:04:58,559
made, like, four grand.

97
00:04:58,646 --> 00:04:59,908
Tommy, Tommy..

98
00:04:59,995 --> 00:05:01,692
- Don't even start.
- With what?

99
00:05:01,779 --> 00:05:04,304
Busting my chops
like you always do.

100
00:05:04,391 --> 00:05:05,653
Well, you don't.

101
00:05:05,740 --> 00:05:07,872
I know what I'm doing.
I'm a professional.

102
00:05:07,959 --> 00:05:09,352
Oh, right.

103
00:05:09,439 --> 00:05:10,875
Taking your 13-year-old
daughter along..

104
00:05:10,962 --> 00:05:12,094
that's very professional.

105
00:05:12,181 --> 00:05:13,922
She's 14

106
00:05:14,009 --> 00:05:17,012
and that's not fair, because
I did not want to bring her.

107
00:05:17,099 --> 00:05:19,362
My psycho ex went to Miami
with her boyfriend

108
00:05:19,449 --> 00:05:21,625
so I got her.

109
00:05:21,712 --> 00:05:23,714
[sighing]
You look good.

110
00:05:23,801 --> 00:05:26,151
You...do something
with your hair?

111
00:05:26,238 --> 00:05:29,981
You should be encouraging me.
I'm trying here.

112
00:05:30,068 --> 00:05:32,157
[scoffing]

113
00:05:32,244 --> 00:05:34,682
Okay. What's the name
of your fugitive?

114
00:05:34,769 --> 00:05:38,076
His name's Carmine O'Brien.
Jumped bail out of St. Louis.

115
00:05:38,163 --> 00:05:41,384
I found out about three days ago
he bought a bus ticket here

116
00:05:41,471 --> 00:05:43,038
so I called this Chief Green

117
00:05:43,125 --> 00:05:45,823
and I asked her to keep
an eye out for him.

118
00:05:45,910 --> 00:05:48,086
I heard on my scanner
she got shot.

119
00:05:48,173 --> 00:05:52,003
So you think the chief found
O'Brien and then he killed her?

120
00:05:52,090 --> 00:05:54,484
- Yeah, I don't know, maybe.
- Why break into her house?

121
00:05:54,571 --> 00:05:56,486
Door was open.

122
00:05:56,573 --> 00:05:59,620
I just went in to find out
what I could about O'Brien.

123
00:05:59,707 --> 00:06:01,883
Okay. When we pick him up,
I'll tell you.

124
00:06:01,970 --> 00:06:05,452
If he had any part in this
murder, I can't give him to you.

125
00:06:05,539 --> 00:06:07,410
What if I get to him first?

126
00:06:07,497 --> 00:06:10,239
- Yeah, right.
- You don't think I can do it?

127
00:06:10,326 --> 00:06:13,373
- No, I don't.
- Fine. We'll see.

128
00:06:13,460 --> 00:06:15,418
- Can you watch Annie?
- Are you kidding?

129
00:06:15,505 --> 00:06:17,115
No. No.

130
00:06:17,202 --> 00:06:19,509
This is really dangerous work
I'm doing.

131
00:06:19,596 --> 00:06:22,251
Your office is a lot safer
than my van, right?

132
00:06:22,338 --> 00:06:24,688
'Besides, she needs
some female time.'

133
00:06:24,775 --> 00:06:27,169
Her mom's such a freaking
wackadoo, and you know

134
00:06:27,256 --> 00:06:29,040
I'm a guy.

135
00:06:31,347 --> 00:06:33,784
- Damn it, Tommy.
- Annie!

136
00:06:33,871 --> 00:06:36,047
'You're spending the day
with your Aunt Teresa!'

137
00:06:36,134 --> 00:06:38,398
- 'Come on! Get your bag!'
- Cool.

138
00:06:38,485 --> 00:06:42,576
It is on,sis.
May the best man win.

139
00:06:45,622 --> 00:06:46,928
Oh, man.

140
00:06:50,322 --> 00:06:52,020
Hey.

141
00:06:52,107 --> 00:06:54,849
Carmine O'Brien
is an accountant from St. Louis.

142
00:06:54,936 --> 00:06:57,068
He was arrested three months
ago for embezzlement

143
00:06:57,155 --> 00:06:59,114
'skipped town
right before the trial.'

144
00:06:59,201 --> 00:07:01,464
Spent summers
growing up in Fairmont.

145
00:07:01,551 --> 00:07:03,118
Might explain
why he's hiding here.

146
00:07:03,205 --> 00:07:04,598
Any history of violence?

147
00:07:04,685 --> 00:07:06,295
No. Strictly white collar.

148
00:07:06,382 --> 00:07:07,644
Ivy League-educated,
no prior arrests.

149
00:07:07,731 --> 00:07:09,951
It's hard to see
this guy shooting a cop.

150
00:07:10,038 --> 00:07:11,518
Doesn't mean he didn't do it.

151
00:07:11,605 --> 00:07:13,781
Have Cho go back to Fairmont
and ask around.

152
00:07:13,868 --> 00:07:15,565
Run his credit card
and phone records

153
00:07:15,652 --> 00:07:17,088
have Rigsby
put out a bolo.

154
00:07:17,175 --> 00:07:18,350
Alright.

155
00:07:19,656 --> 00:07:21,876
- OfficerPrice. Hi.
- Hi.

156
00:07:21,963 --> 00:07:23,486
'Can I help you?'

157
00:07:23,573 --> 00:07:25,532
I felt bad about
not checking that trunk.

158
00:07:25,619 --> 00:07:27,577
Should have caught
that, so, uh..

159
00:07:27,664 --> 00:07:30,232
...I went through
the chief's files.

160
00:07:30,319 --> 00:07:32,756
She pulled over a DUI
day before yesterday..

161
00:07:32,843 --> 00:07:34,105
Russian guy
named Dmitri Zubov.

162
00:07:34,192 --> 00:07:35,890
He's staying at one
of the resorts.

163
00:07:35,977 --> 00:07:37,457
What about him
caught your eye?

164
00:07:37,544 --> 00:07:39,937
He blew a .076
on a breathalyzer.

165
00:07:40,024 --> 00:07:41,765
.76? That's under the limit.

166
00:07:41,852 --> 00:07:44,028
He wasn't drunk, but the chief
arrested him anyway

167
00:07:44,115 --> 00:07:47,118
which is a waste of time,
'cause once it goes to court

168
00:07:47,205 --> 00:07:49,686
the judge is just
gonna throw it out.

169
00:07:49,773 --> 00:07:51,819
She was a real stickler
for details.

170
00:07:51,906 --> 00:07:53,777
Thanks.
We'll check it out.

171
00:07:57,564 --> 00:07:59,740
I want to help out
any way I can.

172
00:07:59,827 --> 00:08:01,437
I know the locals

173
00:08:01,524 --> 00:08:03,221
and I can help out
with interviews.

174
00:08:03,308 --> 00:08:05,223
We'll let you know.

175
00:08:08,923 --> 00:08:10,707
Two fingers.
Just dip and remove.

176
00:08:10,794 --> 00:08:12,927
No hesitation.
Want to give it a try?

177
00:08:13,014 --> 00:08:14,189
Okay.

178
00:08:18,062 --> 00:08:19,934
- Did you feel that?
- Well, just slightly.

179
00:08:20,021 --> 00:08:23,546
- Did you feel that?
- You're good.

180
00:08:23,633 --> 00:08:25,940
Picking pockets. Nice.

181
00:08:26,027 --> 00:08:27,245
I promised I'd show her

182
00:08:27,332 --> 00:08:29,378
if she'd tell me
her Aunty Rees stories.

183
00:08:29,465 --> 00:08:31,293
- Don't you dare.
- Of course not.

184
00:08:31,380 --> 00:08:32,947
I was just stringing him along.

185
00:08:33,034 --> 00:08:35,689
You were, were you?
I guess I won't give you this.

186
00:08:35,776 --> 00:08:38,082
- Hey.
- Annabeth?

187
00:08:38,169 --> 00:08:39,649
- Annie.
- Annie.

188
00:08:39,736 --> 00:08:41,912
Annie,Jane and I
have to go to work.

189
00:08:41,999 --> 00:08:43,435
Mind hanging out
in my office?

190
00:08:43,523 --> 00:08:45,263
Sure.

191
00:08:45,350 --> 00:08:48,876
Rigsby's a nice, easy mark
if you want to keep practicing.

192
00:08:50,312 --> 00:08:52,532
The DUI, Zubov?
He's an economist.

193
00:08:52,619 --> 00:08:54,795
He's in Fairmont for
some sort of trade conference.

194
00:08:54,882 --> 00:08:56,579
He stayed on for vacation.

195
00:08:56,666 --> 00:08:59,103
Fascinating, but not what
you really want to talk about.

196
00:08:59,190 --> 00:09:01,715
I cannot believe
my brother's a bounty hunter.

197
00:09:01,802 --> 00:09:04,195
All of a sudden
he's some sort of tough guy?

198
00:09:04,282 --> 00:09:05,240
Who is he fooling?

199
00:09:05,327 --> 00:09:06,807
Not you.

200
00:09:06,894 --> 00:09:09,157
You know what bugs me?
He didn't tell me.

201
00:09:09,244 --> 00:09:11,202
I'd have told him
it's a bad idea.

202
00:09:11,289 --> 00:09:13,683
He just had to
pick up the phone

203
00:09:13,770 --> 00:09:15,250
but instead, nothing.

204
00:09:15,337 --> 00:09:17,295
I basically raised
that punk and his brothers.

205
00:09:17,382 --> 00:09:19,297
It's not my fault
if he doesn't communicate.

206
00:09:19,384 --> 00:09:20,429
[elevator bell dinging]

207
00:09:20,516 --> 00:09:22,039
You think it ismy fault.

208
00:09:22,126 --> 00:09:24,085
No, I didn't say that.
You said that.

209
00:09:24,172 --> 00:09:26,609
I say live and let live.
You'll all be happier.

210
00:09:26,696 --> 00:09:28,568
Oh, mind your own business.

211
00:09:29,960 --> 00:09:31,701
Last name O'Brien,
first name Carmine.

212
00:09:31,788 --> 00:09:33,485
Gonna e-mail you a picture
right now.

213
00:09:33,573 --> 00:09:36,227
Let me know if there's any hits.
Thanks. Bye.

214
00:09:36,314 --> 00:09:37,751
- Hey.
- Hey.

215
00:09:37,838 --> 00:09:39,970
You just called in
a bolo for O'Brien, right?

216
00:09:40,057 --> 00:09:41,363
Yep.

217
00:09:41,450 --> 00:09:42,973
Nice.

218
00:09:43,060 --> 00:09:45,759
[keyboard keys clacking]

219
00:09:45,846 --> 00:09:48,152
- Can I ask you a question?
- Sure.

220
00:09:48,239 --> 00:09:51,242
Your Sig Sauer, is that a .357,
a .40, or the 9-millimeter?

221
00:09:51,329 --> 00:09:53,331
It's a 9-millimeter.

222
00:09:53,418 --> 00:09:55,377
Great gun.

223
00:09:55,464 --> 00:09:56,596
Thank you.

224
00:09:56,683 --> 00:09:57,684
- Mm-hmm.
- Hey.

225
00:09:57,771 --> 00:09:59,207
Forensics just came back.

226
00:09:59,294 --> 00:10:00,948
No prints off
Chief Green's cruiser.

227
00:10:01,035 --> 00:10:02,863
Killer must have wiped the car.

228
00:10:02,950 --> 00:10:05,126
You got anything
on O'Brien's family in his file?

229
00:10:05,213 --> 00:10:09,478
Uh, his parents are dead.
He's an only child.

230
00:10:09,565 --> 00:10:12,046
If you're looking for leads,
should check the ex-girlfriend.

231
00:10:12,133 --> 00:10:13,787
They have a kid together.

232
00:10:13,874 --> 00:10:16,877
Alright. Thanks.
We'll look into it.

233
00:10:16,964 --> 00:10:18,661
No problem.

234
00:10:21,229 --> 00:10:25,102
- So do you have a girlfriend?
- Yes, I do, as it happens.

235
00:10:25,189 --> 00:10:27,888
- Are you in love with her?
- Oh, good question.

236
00:10:27,975 --> 00:10:29,585
It's hard to say.
I mean..

237
00:10:29,672 --> 00:10:31,892
Is she cute?

238
00:10:31,979 --> 00:10:34,808
You know, maybe you should wait
in your Aunt Teresa's office.

239
00:10:39,856 --> 00:10:41,641
Hey..

240
00:10:41,728 --> 00:10:42,859
[sighing]

241
00:10:48,952 --> 00:10:51,607
[Teresa]
'Mr. Zubov, tell us
about your arrest.'

242
00:10:51,694 --> 00:10:54,131
'I stand charged with a crime
I did not commit.'

243
00:10:54,218 --> 00:10:56,873
Chief Green insisted
I was drunk.

244
00:10:56,960 --> 00:11:00,834
I was not, but she would not
listen to reason.

245
00:11:00,921 --> 00:11:03,619
Did you have any contact with
Chief Green after your arrest?

246
00:11:03,706 --> 00:11:05,403
Can get you something
to drink?

247
00:11:05,490 --> 00:11:07,536
- It's very hot.
- No, thank you, Mr. Zubov.

248
00:11:07,623 --> 00:11:09,451
Just answer the question,
please.

249
00:11:09,538 --> 00:11:12,236
No.
No contact with Chief Green.

250
00:11:12,323 --> 00:11:14,282
'And where were you
last night?'

251
00:11:14,369 --> 00:11:17,764
Last night I had something
to eat, I had a drink.

252
00:11:17,851 --> 00:11:21,724
I had a little more to drink,
but, uh, heh, no driving.

253
00:11:21,811 --> 00:11:24,118
[woman #1]
'Mr. Zubov?'

254
00:11:24,205 --> 00:11:25,641
Are you ready
for your massage?

255
00:11:25,728 --> 00:11:27,643
A new girl. Hello.

256
00:11:28,775 --> 00:11:30,037
Duty calls. Am I done?

257
00:11:30,124 --> 00:11:31,560
Mr. Zubov's gonna
have to reschedule.

258
00:11:31,647 --> 00:11:33,344
Of course.

259
00:11:33,431 --> 00:11:35,085
Now it's all very clear.

260
00:11:35,172 --> 00:11:37,827
You're quite the, uh,
sex fiend, aren't you?

261
00:11:37,914 --> 00:11:39,829
[chuckling]
What do you mean?

262
00:11:39,916 --> 00:11:42,266
Well, you automatically tried
to seduce Agent Lisbon here

263
00:11:42,353 --> 00:11:45,008
but it was the masseuse that
really got your blood pumping.

264
00:11:45,095 --> 00:11:47,271
You're like an owl
watching a mouse.

265
00:11:47,358 --> 00:11:48,838
No. I'm not.

266
00:11:48,925 --> 00:11:50,622
Chief Green thought
you'd committed a crime

267
00:11:50,710 --> 00:11:53,887
but it wasn't drunk driving,
was it? What was it, I wonder?

268
00:11:53,974 --> 00:11:55,671
- This is ridiculous.
- No.

269
00:11:55,758 --> 00:11:58,674
You know what's ridiculous?
Is this. This, uh, ascot..

270
00:11:58,761 --> 00:12:00,589
- Give me this back.
- That's ridiculous. No.

271
00:12:00,676 --> 00:12:02,069
You mind sharing with us

272
00:12:02,156 --> 00:12:04,854
how you got those scratches
on your neck?

273
00:12:04,941 --> 00:12:06,726
I was hiking and boom..
I fell.

274
00:12:06,813 --> 00:12:07,988
[chuckling]

275
00:12:08,075 --> 00:12:09,467
Hiking.

276
00:12:09,554 --> 00:12:10,860
Really?

277
00:12:10,947 --> 00:12:13,036
Yes, hiking.

278
00:12:13,123 --> 00:12:15,996
I refuse to
discuss this further.

279
00:12:18,999 --> 00:12:22,002
Now all we have to do is find
the woman he assaulted.

280
00:12:22,089 --> 00:12:25,353
Well, she's reluctant to make
a public accusation.

281
00:12:25,440 --> 00:12:29,226
That's why, uh, chief hung
the DUI on Zubov.

282
00:12:29,313 --> 00:12:31,751
To buy time to convince
the victim to testify.

283
00:12:31,838 --> 00:12:33,665
It fits.

284
00:12:33,753 --> 00:12:36,756
Butwithout an actual victim,
we don't have anything.

285
00:12:36,843 --> 00:12:39,280
I can't even get
a search warrant for his room.

286
00:12:39,367 --> 00:12:40,934
Zubov's an opportunist.

287
00:12:41,021 --> 00:12:44,154
The question is,
where did he have opportunity?

288
00:12:44,241 --> 00:12:45,155
[knocking]

289
00:12:45,242 --> 00:12:46,461
CBI.

290
00:12:46,548 --> 00:12:49,507
Chad Carmichael,
operations manager here.

291
00:12:49,594 --> 00:12:51,379
What I can I do for you?

292
00:12:51,466 --> 00:12:54,208
We're investigating a crime that
relates to one of your guests

293
00:12:54,295 --> 00:12:55,470
Dmitri Zubov.

294
00:12:55,557 --> 00:12:57,951
Oh. What did he do?

295
00:12:58,038 --> 00:13:01,215
We're not at liberty to say,
but what we're gonna need is

296
00:13:01,302 --> 00:13:04,044
a list of your staff who've
been in Mr. Zubov's room

297
00:13:04,131 --> 00:13:05,785
and security camera
footage

298
00:13:05,872 --> 00:13:07,525
from the hallway
outside his door.

299
00:13:07,612 --> 00:13:11,747
Uh, that's problematic.
Mr. Zubov is a valued guest.

300
00:13:11,834 --> 00:13:13,444
It's cold in here.

301
00:13:13,531 --> 00:13:16,708
Is-is that your, uh,
own personal air conditioner?

302
00:13:16,796 --> 00:13:18,362
Uh, yes.

303
00:13:18,449 --> 00:13:21,191
Fancy. A place like this
doesn't have central air?

304
00:13:22,540 --> 00:13:24,847
I guess I just like it cold.

305
00:13:24,934 --> 00:13:27,328
What's going on here?

306
00:13:27,415 --> 00:13:28,895
[sighing]
Dad.

307
00:13:28,982 --> 00:13:30,592
This is my father,
Philip Carmichael.

308
00:13:30,679 --> 00:13:33,247
- 'He owns the resort.'
- Government people, are you?

309
00:13:33,334 --> 00:13:34,944
These people are with CBI.

310
00:13:35,031 --> 00:13:38,295
They need information
about a guest.

311
00:13:38,382 --> 00:13:41,081
And you didn't call me?

312
00:13:41,168 --> 00:13:43,170
It is myjob.
I'm handling it.

313
00:13:43,257 --> 00:13:44,867
[Philip clearing throat]

314
00:13:44,954 --> 00:13:47,652
We're happy to assist
law enforcement at any time.

315
00:13:47,739 --> 00:13:49,393
We just need a search warrant.

316
00:13:49,480 --> 00:13:52,483
I can't give you the details,
but Mr. Zubov may be involved

317
00:13:52,570 --> 00:13:56,270
in the murder of Chief Green.
This is extremely important.

318
00:13:56,357 --> 00:13:58,228
- Oh, my god. Really?
- And I sympathize.

319
00:13:58,315 --> 00:14:01,144
But we have to respect
the privacy of our guests.

320
00:14:01,231 --> 00:14:04,974
Son, show them out.
And next time, call.

321
00:14:11,502 --> 00:14:13,896
Does the old tyrant always
talk to you like that?

322
00:14:15,680 --> 00:14:19,119
So you're thinking maybe
Zubov killed Chief Green?

323
00:14:19,206 --> 00:14:22,165
Yes, possibly.

324
00:14:22,252 --> 00:14:24,211
I'll get the video for you.
Wait here.

325
00:14:24,298 --> 00:14:25,647
Thank you, chad.

326
00:14:25,734 --> 00:14:28,171
Not easy with a father like
that, but thank you.

327
00:14:28,258 --> 00:14:29,825
Appreciate it.

328
00:14:33,350 --> 00:14:34,830
[door opening]

329
00:14:35,962 --> 00:14:37,180
Mmm.

330
00:14:37,267 --> 00:14:39,139
- 'You still in Fairmont?'
- Yeah.

331
00:14:39,226 --> 00:14:41,532
Go to 787 Elm Street.
O'Brien's there right now.

332
00:14:41,619 --> 00:14:43,056
How'd you get the address?

333
00:14:43,143 --> 00:14:45,362
His ex has been getting calls
from a cell.

334
00:14:45,449 --> 00:14:47,625
We accessed that cell's GPS
and pulled the location.

335
00:14:47,712 --> 00:14:49,018
Got it.

336
00:15:02,075 --> 00:15:04,251
O'Brien!

337
00:15:04,338 --> 00:15:06,079
O'Brien! CBI! Don't move!

338
00:15:07,254 --> 00:15:08,385
Hey!

339
00:15:10,953 --> 00:15:12,172
[car horn honking]

340
00:15:12,259 --> 00:15:13,390
[tires screeching]

341
00:15:15,392 --> 00:15:17,264
[gasping]

342
00:15:20,658 --> 00:15:23,313
[groaning]
Ow!

343
00:15:23,400 --> 00:15:25,098
You okay?

344
00:15:28,188 --> 00:15:30,494
[panting]

345
00:15:35,891 --> 00:15:38,459
It's either a sprained muscle in
your back or a ruptured disc.

346
00:15:38,546 --> 00:15:40,374
They'll tell you
at the hospital.

347
00:15:40,461 --> 00:15:42,202
- I'm fine.
- Go to the hospital!

348
00:15:42,289 --> 00:15:43,333
[cellphone ringing]

349
00:15:43,420 --> 00:15:45,857
- Yeah, okay.
- What's up?

350
00:15:45,945 --> 00:15:47,685
'I've been going through
the security footage'

351
00:15:47,772 --> 00:15:50,950
and I may have found
the woman Zubov assaulted.

352
00:15:51,037 --> 00:15:54,736
It's a maid. She's crying,
and her uniform is torn.

353
00:15:54,823 --> 00:15:58,087
Work schedule says her name
is Sofia Chavez.

354
00:15:58,174 --> 00:16:00,698
Alright. Bring her in.

355
00:16:00,785 --> 00:16:03,136
- How's your guy?
- He's hurt pretty bad.

356
00:16:03,223 --> 00:16:05,616
- Yeah, looked pretty rough.
- You shouldn't have been here.

357
00:16:05,703 --> 00:16:07,749
I told you I was
going after O'Brien.

358
00:16:07,836 --> 00:16:09,794
I mean, stuff happens
when you're chasing guys.

359
00:16:09,881 --> 00:16:12,014
It could have been me
that got knocked.

360
00:16:12,101 --> 00:16:13,798
Your daughter got shot
this morning

361
00:16:13,885 --> 00:16:15,583
I've got a guy
in the hospital

362
00:16:15,670 --> 00:16:17,367
because you don't know
what you're doing.

363
00:16:17,454 --> 00:16:19,413
Oh, like hell, I don't.

364
00:16:19,500 --> 00:16:21,502
You know how I got O'Brien?

365
00:16:21,589 --> 00:16:24,026
He's a Type 1 Diabetic,
and I paid the pharmacist

366
00:16:24,113 --> 00:16:26,289
to tell me when he comes
to buy insulin.

367
00:16:26,376 --> 00:16:28,596
That's skill.
Your people think of that?

368
00:16:28,683 --> 00:16:30,902
Somebody could have
gotten killed.

369
00:16:30,990 --> 00:16:33,166
I love you, but..

370
00:16:33,253 --> 00:16:35,037
"I love you, but.."
But what, sis?

371
00:16:35,124 --> 00:16:38,214
"But...you're a loser. You'll
always be a loser. Just quit."

372
00:16:38,301 --> 00:16:41,304
I love you, but you and Annabeth
need to go home.

373
00:16:41,391 --> 00:16:44,090
Tommy, you should think
about going back to school

374
00:16:44,177 --> 00:16:47,006
learn a trade.
You always liked electronics.

375
00:16:47,093 --> 00:16:50,270
Okay, sure.
Trade school it is.

376
00:16:50,357 --> 00:16:54,361
You want me to detail your car
for you before I go?

377
00:16:54,448 --> 00:16:55,927
Agent Lisbon,
we've set up roadblocks

378
00:16:56,015 --> 00:16:57,973
and we're sending officers
to look for O'Brien.

379
00:16:58,060 --> 00:17:01,759
- 'You want to talk to 'em?'
- We'll finish this later.

380
00:17:07,983 --> 00:17:09,854
I have nothing to say.

381
00:17:09,941 --> 00:17:12,205
I go in room,
I clean, I leave.

382
00:17:12,292 --> 00:17:13,684
Wait.

383
00:17:13,771 --> 00:17:16,644
Zubov didn't assault you?
Didn't hurt you?

384
00:17:16,731 --> 00:17:17,862
No.

385
00:17:19,777 --> 00:17:23,390
Sofia, I don't work
for immigration.

386
00:17:23,477 --> 00:17:26,349
Nothing's gonna happen to you.
I promise.

387
00:17:29,613 --> 00:17:32,268
So this is just us?

388
00:17:32,355 --> 00:17:33,661
No police?

389
00:17:35,271 --> 00:17:36,403
No.

390
00:17:36,490 --> 00:17:37,839
Just us.

391
00:17:39,710 --> 00:17:42,539
[sighing]
I clean room.

392
00:17:42,626 --> 00:17:45,455
I think I alone.

393
00:17:45,542 --> 00:17:48,676
He come out of bathroom.

394
00:17:48,763 --> 00:17:51,113
He put hand on me. He..

395
00:17:51,200 --> 00:17:54,943
He rip my, um, this.

396
00:17:55,030 --> 00:17:59,121
- He ripped your uniform.
- Yes.

397
00:17:59,208 --> 00:18:01,036
I scared. I run for door.

398
00:18:01,123 --> 00:18:03,647
He grab me.

399
00:18:03,734 --> 00:18:06,389
I fight.

400
00:18:06,476 --> 00:18:08,565
I get out.

401
00:18:08,652 --> 00:18:10,524
Who told Chief Green
about it?

402
00:18:12,221 --> 00:18:14,571
I told.

403
00:18:14,658 --> 00:18:18,358
She was my friend.

404
00:18:18,445 --> 00:18:24,103
She tell me to accuse Zubov,
but I say no.

405
00:18:24,190 --> 00:18:26,888
She say she keep him
until I change my mind..

406
00:18:29,717 --> 00:18:31,588
...but I no change.

407
00:18:35,201 --> 00:18:36,985
He kill her?

408
00:18:37,072 --> 00:18:39,248
It's a possibility.

409
00:18:39,335 --> 00:18:43,383
That's why it's so important
for you to come forward.

410
00:18:43,470 --> 00:18:45,907
Why?

411
00:18:45,994 --> 00:18:48,692
The rich, they get away
with everything.

412
00:18:52,087 --> 00:18:54,002
[sighing]

413
00:18:54,089 --> 00:18:55,873
Any luck finding O'Brien?

414
00:18:55,960 --> 00:18:58,180
- Look--
- We're leaving tomorrow.

415
00:18:58,267 --> 00:19:01,270
Maybe you're right. Maybe
I'm not cut out for this.

416
00:19:01,357 --> 00:19:02,837
Really?

417
00:19:02,924 --> 00:19:05,144
Yeah, really. What business
do I have bounty hunting?

418
00:19:05,231 --> 00:19:07,929
Truth is, it's not the first
time I thought about quitting.

419
00:19:08,016 --> 00:19:10,236
- Tommy..
- It's probably for the best.

420
00:19:10,323 --> 00:19:12,890
Annabeth will dismember me if we
leave without saying good-bye.

421
00:19:12,977 --> 00:19:14,544
You want to
get lunch tomorrow?

422
00:19:14,631 --> 00:19:16,981
Sure. Yeah.

423
00:19:17,068 --> 00:19:18,983
[door opening]

424
00:19:20,855 --> 00:19:22,465
[man #2]
'This is absurd.'

425
00:19:22,552 --> 00:19:25,120
There is no victim of
an assault. Where is she?

426
00:19:25,207 --> 00:19:27,557
Well, there is a victim.
Sofia Chavez.

427
00:19:27,644 --> 00:19:30,256
Victim? Please.

428
00:19:30,343 --> 00:19:32,171
I ask her to touch me--

429
00:19:32,258 --> 00:19:33,998
- Dmitri..
- It's okay. It's okay.

430
00:19:34,085 --> 00:19:36,914
I ask. She refuses.
That's all.

431
00:19:37,001 --> 00:19:38,786
I only ask her

432
00:19:38,873 --> 00:19:41,528
because my masseuse that day
was little bit ugly, you know?

433
00:19:41,615 --> 00:19:44,487
I see. And normally
you assault your masseuse?

434
00:19:44,574 --> 00:19:47,838
[scoffing]
You make it sound so crude.

435
00:19:47,925 --> 00:19:52,016
I love women.
And love is beautiful, no?

436
00:19:52,103 --> 00:19:53,931
Alright. You have
no case here, agent.

437
00:19:54,018 --> 00:19:55,411
Unless there's
anything else...

438
00:19:55,498 --> 00:19:57,239
Mr. Zubov, we checked
the security footage.

439
00:19:57,326 --> 00:19:59,067
You weren't back
until after 12:00

440
00:19:59,154 --> 00:20:00,634
the night of
Chief Green's murder.

441
00:20:00,721 --> 00:20:02,679
- Where were you?
- You don't have to answer.

442
00:20:02,766 --> 00:20:05,682
We'll find out where you were.
It's just a question of time.

443
00:20:08,598 --> 00:20:10,470
[speaking indistinctly]

444
00:20:12,559 --> 00:20:14,648
I went to Chief Green's home.

445
00:20:14,735 --> 00:20:17,041
- Son of a bitch.
- To discuss my arrest.

446
00:20:17,128 --> 00:20:19,000
To see if something
could be done.

447
00:20:19,087 --> 00:20:21,872
[chuckling]
It's starting to become
a bit tedious here.

448
00:20:21,959 --> 00:20:23,613
You went to bribe her?

449
00:20:23,700 --> 00:20:26,573
I was hoping to find a mutual
acceptable resolution.

450
00:20:26,660 --> 00:20:29,445
But a friend
of the chief's arrives.

451
00:20:29,532 --> 00:20:30,968
A big woman.

452
00:20:31,055 --> 00:20:34,102
Uh, Jori. Jori,
I think her name was.

453
00:20:34,189 --> 00:20:38,062
She was upset.
About what, I don't know.

454
00:20:38,149 --> 00:20:40,413
- And I left.
- Jori?

455
00:20:40,500 --> 00:20:42,197
Must be Jori Kasser.

456
00:20:42,284 --> 00:20:45,374
Uh, the Russian was with
Chief Green when I got there

457
00:20:45,461 --> 00:20:47,071
but he left right away.

458
00:20:47,158 --> 00:20:49,857
What were you doing that late
at the chief's house?

459
00:20:49,944 --> 00:20:51,728
Chief Green
had left a message.

460
00:20:51,815 --> 00:20:53,774
Wanted to know
where my son Steven was.

461
00:20:53,861 --> 00:20:56,646
You know why
she was looking for him?

462
00:20:56,733 --> 00:20:58,169
Steven has
some drug problems.

463
00:20:58,257 --> 00:20:59,954
Knows a bit about
Fairmont's seedy side.

464
00:21:00,041 --> 00:21:02,739
Chief would go to him for
information from time to time.

465
00:21:02,826 --> 00:21:04,306
Chief Green said
that a fugitive

466
00:21:04,393 --> 00:21:06,090
might be hiding out
in Fairmont

467
00:21:06,177 --> 00:21:08,876
and wanted to know if Steven
had heard anything about him.

468
00:21:08,963 --> 00:21:11,531
Why not call?
Why go in person?

469
00:21:11,618 --> 00:21:13,315
I needed to ask a favor.

470
00:21:13,402 --> 00:21:17,450
Um, I'd overheard Steven say

471
00:21:17,537 --> 00:21:20,931
that he was going up
to a cabin in the woods.

472
00:21:21,018 --> 00:21:23,543
'I know what he does there.
He buys drugs.'

473
00:21:23,630 --> 00:21:27,286
And I asked the chief,
if that was what he was doing

474
00:21:27,373 --> 00:21:29,070
to get him
into a treatment program.

475
00:21:29,157 --> 00:21:30,637
He really wants to get clean.

476
00:21:30,724 --> 00:21:32,987
We need to speak to your son.
Where's he?

477
00:21:33,074 --> 00:21:37,905
[sighing]
That's the thing.

478
00:21:37,992 --> 00:21:40,690
I haven't heard from Steven
since I talked to the chief.

479
00:21:40,777 --> 00:21:43,606
Steve's missing?

480
00:21:43,693 --> 00:21:46,305
Why didn't you say
anything?

481
00:21:46,392 --> 00:21:49,003
I was hoping
it was a coincidence.

482
00:21:49,090 --> 00:21:50,961
Sometimes he disappears.

483
00:21:52,920 --> 00:21:55,139
Do you think your son
had something to do

484
00:21:55,226 --> 00:21:57,098
with the murder
of Chief Green?

485
00:21:58,534 --> 00:22:00,841
[voice breaking]
No, not if he was sober.

486
00:22:03,974 --> 00:22:06,020
Hey, boss.
Jori Kasser says her son

487
00:22:06,107 --> 00:22:07,630
might've been involved
in the murder.

488
00:22:07,717 --> 00:22:09,893
Apparently he was buying drugs
up at some cabin.

489
00:22:09,980 --> 00:22:12,243
- Gonna check it out.
- Call my cell if anything.

490
00:22:12,331 --> 00:22:14,071
I'm gonna be out of the office.

491
00:22:14,158 --> 00:22:16,422
- Anything on Zubov?
- Yeah, Van Pelt's on it.

492
00:22:17,771 --> 00:22:20,121
- Yeah, thanks.
- Problem?

493
00:22:20,208 --> 00:22:23,951
M.E. puts the time of death
between 2:00 and 3:00 a.m.

494
00:22:24,038 --> 00:22:25,996
Zubov was in his room
from midnight on.

495
00:22:26,083 --> 00:22:28,216
- He couldn't be the killer.
- Mm.

496
00:22:28,303 --> 00:22:29,739
He was a non-starter anyhow.

497
00:22:29,826 --> 00:22:32,089
And Sofia Chavez
won't testify against him.

498
00:22:32,176 --> 00:22:33,613
We can't even touch
the scumbag.

499
00:22:33,700 --> 00:22:35,963
The world's full of scumbags
we can't touch.

500
00:22:36,050 --> 00:22:37,704
I know, I know.
It's just..

501
00:22:37,791 --> 00:22:40,315
I hear you. It'd soothe
your troubled soul

502
00:22:40,402 --> 00:22:43,144
if you could just stick it
to this particular scumbag.

503
00:22:43,231 --> 00:22:46,147
Well, yeah. I guess
it kind of would.

504
00:22:46,234 --> 00:22:47,975
Shall we?

505
00:22:53,023 --> 00:22:54,285
[car door closing]

506
00:22:54,373 --> 00:22:55,983
They're, uh, rental cabins
for vacationers.

507
00:22:56,070 --> 00:22:58,072
But they're being
renovated now.

508
00:22:58,159 --> 00:23:01,031
Pretty isolated.
Get many drug buys up here?

509
00:23:01,118 --> 00:23:03,033
Heard rumors there were.

510
00:23:03,120 --> 00:23:06,080
Hard to imagine Steve
hanging out in these parts.

511
00:23:06,167 --> 00:23:08,125
He's not what you'd call
a country boy.

512
00:23:08,212 --> 00:23:10,084
That pile of leaves there.

513
00:23:13,217 --> 00:23:15,089
Who's raking leaves up here?

514
00:23:19,180 --> 00:23:20,355
Phew!

515
00:23:22,575 --> 00:23:25,447
[sighing and sniffling]

516
00:23:31,410 --> 00:23:33,847
Steve Kasser?

517
00:23:33,934 --> 00:23:36,458
I better call his mother.

518
00:23:36,545 --> 00:23:38,242
Yeah.

519
00:23:38,329 --> 00:23:41,202
[indistinct conversation]

520
00:23:51,952 --> 00:23:53,867
Mr. Zubov?

521
00:23:53,954 --> 00:23:56,086
Are you ready
for your massage?

522
00:23:56,173 --> 00:23:57,610
Ah, very nice.

523
00:23:57,697 --> 00:23:59,699
Yes, please.
Uh, lead the way.

524
00:24:13,190 --> 00:24:15,932
[cellphone ringing]

525
00:24:16,019 --> 00:24:17,194
Hmm.

526
00:24:17,281 --> 00:24:20,154
[ringing continues]

527
00:24:20,241 --> 00:24:22,025
Rigsby. What's the word?

528
00:24:22,112 --> 00:24:23,505
Lisbon's not answering
her phone.

529
00:24:23,592 --> 00:24:26,160
- Any idea where she is?
- Nope.

530
00:24:26,247 --> 00:24:28,423
We got another vic
dead by a rental cabin.

531
00:24:28,510 --> 00:24:29,772
Maybe connected
to Chief Green.

532
00:24:29,859 --> 00:24:31,600
- Drug thing, looks like.
- Cocaine?

533
00:24:31,687 --> 00:24:33,689
Yeah. Victim had
about five grams on him.

534
00:24:33,776 --> 00:24:35,604
Hmm. Is there just
one cabin

535
00:24:35,691 --> 00:24:37,650
or are others nearby?

536
00:24:37,737 --> 00:24:38,694
There's a few.

537
00:24:38,781 --> 00:24:40,217
[clattering]

538
00:24:40,304 --> 00:24:42,045
[Zubov yelling indistinctly]

539
00:24:42,132 --> 00:24:44,874
[Zubov]
'I-I made a mistake!
I didn't know that..'

540
00:24:44,961 --> 00:24:47,181
Uh, gotta go.
I'll see you up there later.

541
00:24:47,268 --> 00:24:50,445
- 'If I knew..'
- What?

542
00:24:50,532 --> 00:24:52,969
[Van Pelt]
You're under arrest
for solicitation

543
00:24:53,056 --> 00:24:54,928
sexual assault,
assault on a police officer..

544
00:24:55,015 --> 00:24:56,190
Wait, please..

545
00:24:56,277 --> 00:24:57,844
You've the right
to remain silent.

546
00:24:57,931 --> 00:25:00,455
Anything you say can and will
be used against you

547
00:25:00,542 --> 00:25:01,761
in a court of law.

548
00:25:01,848 --> 00:25:04,241
[gunshots]

549
00:25:09,072 --> 00:25:11,510
Nice shooting.

550
00:25:11,597 --> 00:25:14,077
I practice a lot
on the gun range with dad.

551
00:25:15,992 --> 00:25:18,212
It's good that you spend time
with your dad

552
00:25:18,299 --> 00:25:20,649
'but you should do other
stuff too. Kid stuff.'

553
00:25:20,736 --> 00:25:22,912
Why? I already know
what I wanna do.

554
00:25:22,999 --> 00:25:24,261
Really? What's that?

555
00:25:24,348 --> 00:25:27,308
I wanna be a cop.
Like you.

556
00:25:27,395 --> 00:25:28,788
I'm flattered. I am.

557
00:25:28,875 --> 00:25:31,312
I don't think you really
know what you want yet.

558
00:25:31,399 --> 00:25:32,966
You don't have to.
It's okay.

559
00:25:33,053 --> 00:25:35,882
- Yeah, I do.
- I sleep five hours a night.

560
00:25:35,969 --> 00:25:39,189
I haven't been able to get away
to see you and your dad

561
00:25:39,276 --> 00:25:42,279
and your uncles in over a year.
That's not what you want.

562
00:25:42,366 --> 00:25:44,978
Aunt Teresa, you get paid
to carry a Glock.

563
00:25:45,065 --> 00:25:47,546
You beat up people
when they get out of line.

564
00:25:47,633 --> 00:25:52,028
- You're totally badass.
- My point still stands.

565
00:25:52,115 --> 00:25:53,290
Come on.

566
00:25:53,377 --> 00:25:55,945
Come on. Come on.

567
00:26:02,865 --> 00:26:04,824
You got a text
while you were gone.

568
00:26:04,911 --> 00:26:06,434
- I did?
- Yeah.

569
00:26:06,521 --> 00:26:08,392
- How'd you do?
- I kicked butt.

570
00:26:08,479 --> 00:26:10,220
Yes, she did.

571
00:26:11,657 --> 00:26:14,703
I gotta go back to work.

572
00:26:14,790 --> 00:26:17,097
- Already?
- Yeah.

573
00:26:22,537 --> 00:26:23,756
Keep in touch.

574
00:26:23,843 --> 00:26:25,279
Absolutely, Rees.

575
00:26:25,366 --> 00:26:27,890
I'll call you
when I learn that trade.

576
00:26:27,977 --> 00:26:29,457
- Bye.
- Bye.

577
00:26:29,544 --> 00:26:31,198
[buttons beeping]

578
00:26:32,373 --> 00:26:34,897
Hey, Rigs.
I got your text.

579
00:26:34,984 --> 00:26:37,334
'Did you find Steve Kasser?'

580
00:26:37,421 --> 00:26:39,206
Yeah, he's been dead
a couple days.

581
00:26:39,293 --> 00:26:42,165
'Damn. That's a shame.
Did the coroner show up?'

582
00:26:42,252 --> 00:26:44,124
'Nope. They should be soon.'

583
00:26:49,477 --> 00:26:50,870
[Wayne]
'Those are exit wounds.'

584
00:26:50,957 --> 00:26:52,219
'Steve was shot twice.
Killer used a .380.'

585
00:26:52,306 --> 00:26:54,047
- Same caliber as Chief Green.
- Yeah.

586
00:26:54,134 --> 00:26:56,702
There's more blood over there.
Chief Green's, I'm betting.

587
00:26:56,789 --> 00:26:59,139
So Chief Green comes here
looking for Steve.

588
00:26:59,226 --> 00:27:01,445
Steve's buying coke
from a dealer.

589
00:27:01,532 --> 00:27:02,751
The dealer sees the chief

590
00:27:02,838 --> 00:27:04,797
freaks out and kills
both her and Steve.

591
00:27:04,884 --> 00:27:06,799
He dumps Chief Green
in her police cruiser

592
00:27:06,886 --> 00:27:08,278
and hides Steve here.

593
00:27:08,365 --> 00:27:09,802
Makes sense,
but that scenario

594
00:27:09,889 --> 00:27:11,847
pretty much eliminates
O'Brien as a suspect.

595
00:27:11,934 --> 00:27:14,371
And whatever an Ivy League
accountant was doing in town

596
00:27:14,458 --> 00:27:15,764
he wasn't doing coke.

597
00:27:15,851 --> 00:27:17,461
So he's not the killer.

598
00:27:17,548 --> 00:27:18,811
Why is Philip Carmichael here?

599
00:27:18,898 --> 00:27:21,509
'He owns the cabins.
He's here to let us in.'

600
00:27:21,596 --> 00:27:23,293
Give a yell
if you need anything.

601
00:27:23,380 --> 00:27:24,555
- Okay.
- Have you seen Jane?

602
00:27:24,643 --> 00:27:26,557
Says he'll be up here later.

603
00:28:01,201 --> 00:28:02,332
[unzipping bag]

604
00:28:40,544 --> 00:28:42,024
Will this take long?

605
00:28:42,111 --> 00:28:44,244
It'll take as long
as it takes.

606
00:28:44,331 --> 00:28:46,333
Hey, check it out.

607
00:28:46,420 --> 00:28:48,857
- Someone was staying here.
- Yeah. Recently.

608
00:28:48,944 --> 00:28:50,554
Lot of sugar-free stuff.

609
00:28:50,641 --> 00:28:52,252
O'Brien was a diabetic.

610
00:28:52,339 --> 00:28:54,776
- He could have been here.
- How'd he end up here?

611
00:28:54,863 --> 00:28:57,300
Well, a lot of people knew
these cabins were empty.

612
00:28:57,387 --> 00:29:00,477
Not a bad place
to hide out.

613
00:29:00,564 --> 00:29:02,001
You think he witnessed
the murders?

614
00:29:02,088 --> 00:29:03,219
Maybe.

615
00:29:04,133 --> 00:29:05,569
'Maybe.'

616
00:29:05,656 --> 00:29:09,356
Question is,
where is he now?

617
00:29:13,186 --> 00:29:14,927
But the roadblocks
are still up, right?

618
00:29:15,014 --> 00:29:17,930
Let us know
if you get a hit.

619
00:29:18,017 --> 00:29:19,453
Nothing on O'Brien
from the airport

620
00:29:19,540 --> 00:29:21,629
bus station,
or the train station.

621
00:29:21,716 --> 00:29:23,631
Hey. Welcome back.

622
00:29:25,546 --> 00:29:28,157
[Wayne]
'Doctors say what
the problem is?'

623
00:29:28,244 --> 00:29:30,638
Yeah.
I got hit by a car.

624
00:29:30,725 --> 00:29:32,379
Cho. Good to have you back.

625
00:29:32,466 --> 00:29:33,467
[exhaling]
Thanks.

626
00:29:33,554 --> 00:29:35,338
I got a call from a ranger.

627
00:29:35,425 --> 00:29:37,906
He spotted a man driving down
Black Canyon Fire Road

628
00:29:37,993 --> 00:29:39,429
thirty miles
outside of Fairmont.

629
00:29:39,516 --> 00:29:41,736
'Caucasian, male,
50s, grey hair..'

630
00:29:41,823 --> 00:29:44,260
Sounds like O'Brien.
We're on it.

631
00:29:44,347 --> 00:29:46,828
Uh, Van Pelt, why don't
you go with Rigsby?

632
00:29:55,228 --> 00:29:59,841
Uh, about a mile up ahead
turn right onto the fire road.

633
00:29:59,928 --> 00:30:01,103
Okay.

634
00:30:03,932 --> 00:30:05,716
Lisbon's niece,
sharp girl.

635
00:30:05,804 --> 00:30:09,546
- Yeah, I guess.
- Yeah. Good questions.

636
00:30:09,633 --> 00:30:11,287
- Yeah.
- Do you love her?

637
00:30:11,374 --> 00:30:13,246
What, Annabeth?

638
00:30:13,333 --> 00:30:16,466
- Your girlfriend Sarah.
- Oh, right.

639
00:30:16,553 --> 00:30:20,557
- So?
- I don't see why it matters.

640
00:30:20,644 --> 00:30:21,820
Uh-oh.

641
00:30:21,907 --> 00:30:23,647
Look, we have
a good time together

642
00:30:23,734 --> 00:30:26,433
we enjoy each other's company,
I look forward to seeing her.

643
00:30:26,520 --> 00:30:28,217
Isn't that enough?
Why worry about it?

644
00:30:28,304 --> 00:30:31,090
Trust me,
she's worrying about it.

645
00:30:31,177 --> 00:30:33,570
[sighing]
I just think if you start
talking like that

646
00:30:33,657 --> 00:30:35,398
you're gonna get hurt.

647
00:30:39,489 --> 00:30:41,840
I'm not sure I even know
what that means.

648
00:30:41,927 --> 00:30:44,843
"I love you."
What does that say, really?

649
00:30:44,930 --> 00:30:47,933
I don't know, Wayne.

650
00:30:48,020 --> 00:30:50,152
My last relationship
didn't exactly end well.

651
00:30:50,239 --> 00:30:54,678
I'm probably not the best
person to ask right now.

652
00:30:54,765 --> 00:30:56,680
Fair enough.

653
00:30:57,943 --> 00:30:59,683
There's your right.

654
00:31:05,864 --> 00:31:07,213
[Wayne]
'What the hell!'

655
00:31:07,300 --> 00:31:08,910
[brakes squealing]

656
00:31:09,563 --> 00:31:10,956
Tommy!

657
00:31:11,043 --> 00:31:13,828
Put the gun away, Tommy.
Put the weapon away.

658
00:31:13,915 --> 00:31:15,047
Holster it!

659
00:31:22,097 --> 00:31:24,404
Uh, who are you now?

660
00:31:35,023 --> 00:31:36,720
Hey, what's going on?

661
00:31:36,807 --> 00:31:39,114
O'Brien won't tell us
what he witnessed.

662
00:31:39,201 --> 00:31:41,203
His lawyer won't be here
for a while.

663
00:31:41,290 --> 00:31:43,945
Let him stew. But he's a runner.
Keep him on lockdown.

664
00:31:44,032 --> 00:31:46,034
Okay.

665
00:31:46,121 --> 00:31:47,993
Boss? They just put him
in your office.

666
00:32:01,049 --> 00:32:02,529
I know how you got O'Brien.

667
00:32:02,616 --> 00:32:05,924
The tech guys did
a diagnostic on my phone.

668
00:32:06,011 --> 00:32:07,795
You downloaded spyware

669
00:32:07,882 --> 00:32:09,536
so you could listen
to my conversations.

670
00:32:09,623 --> 00:32:11,755
Sorry.

671
00:32:11,842 --> 00:32:14,889
You couldn't get him yourself,
so you piggybacked on us.

672
00:32:14,976 --> 00:32:18,980
[sighing]
I'm broke, Rees.

673
00:32:19,067 --> 00:32:21,940
Alimony, rent,
friggin' eighth grade prom.

674
00:32:22,027 --> 00:32:24,290
Can you even believe
they have that?

675
00:32:24,377 --> 00:32:25,726
I needed this guy.

676
00:32:25,813 --> 00:32:28,163
So you lied
and cheated your own sister.

677
00:32:28,250 --> 00:32:31,601
I'd really appreciate it
if you give him to me.

678
00:32:31,688 --> 00:32:35,083
- Are you out of your mind?
- I need a favor.

679
00:32:35,170 --> 00:32:38,086
Do you think I'd give you
O'Brien after what you pulled?

680
00:32:38,173 --> 00:32:40,871
Not to mention the fact
that he might be a witness.

681
00:32:40,959 --> 00:32:42,917
Do you even know
how hard this is?

682
00:32:43,004 --> 00:32:45,920
Okay, I am doing you a favor
by not arresting you.

683
00:32:46,007 --> 00:32:49,228
Now go do something
different with your life.

684
00:32:49,315 --> 00:32:51,491
No, you don't tell me
how to live.

685
00:32:51,578 --> 00:32:52,622
Tommy, come on.

686
00:32:52,709 --> 00:32:54,189
I bust my ass every day

687
00:32:54,276 --> 00:32:57,801
to put food on the table
for me and my kid by myself.

688
00:32:57,888 --> 00:33:00,761
Hey, maybe I haven't done
quite as well as you have

689
00:33:00,848 --> 00:33:02,806
but I'm doing
the best that I can

690
00:33:02,893 --> 00:33:04,808
so don't tell me
how to live.

691
00:33:18,213 --> 00:33:19,693
- I'm sorry.
- Excuse me. Sorry.

692
00:33:19,780 --> 00:33:21,521
Sorry about that.

693
00:33:30,921 --> 00:33:32,053
Hello.

694
00:33:35,143 --> 00:33:36,362
[elevator bell dinging]

695
00:33:36,449 --> 00:33:38,842
- Where are we going?
- Uh, Tommy.

696
00:33:38,929 --> 00:33:41,584
- Here's O'Brien, he's yours.
- What?

697
00:33:41,671 --> 00:33:44,587
Go get your bounty.
But you have to leave right now.

698
00:33:44,674 --> 00:33:46,894
Excuse me. I'm very confused.
What is going on?

699
00:33:46,981 --> 00:33:49,114
Annie...pick her up
at the Ellington Inn.

700
00:33:49,201 --> 00:33:52,204
- Isn't she at the motel?
- No, I got her a spa package..

701
00:33:52,291 --> 00:33:54,119
...facial, massage, the works.
She'll be waiting.

702
00:33:54,206 --> 00:33:57,122
- How do you know my daughter?
- Give her my best.

703
00:34:02,127 --> 00:34:03,606
Lisbon.

704
00:34:03,693 --> 00:34:05,652
Are you sure we can't get
O'Brien's public..

705
00:34:05,739 --> 00:34:06,870
- Lisbon.
- ...here any sooner?

706
00:34:06,957 --> 00:34:08,568
No, I..

707
00:34:08,655 --> 00:34:10,613
- What're you doing?
- We've to leave now.

708
00:34:10,700 --> 00:34:13,138
- I need to talk to O'Brien.
- That might be difficult.

709
00:34:13,225 --> 00:34:14,965
- He's not in the building.
- Why not?

710
00:34:15,053 --> 00:34:17,011
Uh, I'll explain to you
on the road.

711
00:34:17,098 --> 00:34:19,448
- I know a great shortcut.
- Where to?

712
00:34:22,321 --> 00:34:24,758
Chad, it's Agent Lisbon
from the CBI.

713
00:34:24,845 --> 00:34:26,281
We need your help.

714
00:34:26,368 --> 00:34:27,935
Yeah, sure, of course.

715
00:34:28,022 --> 00:34:30,503
There's a bounty hunter
on his way to your hotel

716
00:34:30,590 --> 00:34:33,636
to pick up his daughter.
He's traveling with a fugitive.

717
00:34:33,723 --> 00:34:35,421
Wait, that guy
squatting in our cabin?

718
00:34:35,508 --> 00:34:37,118
- My dad was just mentioning--
- Listen..

719
00:34:37,205 --> 00:34:39,164
...tell your father
to get security.

720
00:34:39,251 --> 00:34:41,601
Detain him. We'll be there
in 20 minutes.

721
00:34:56,398 --> 00:34:58,313
[inhaling sharply]

722
00:34:58,400 --> 00:35:00,881
Well, that was
very well played.

723
00:35:03,884 --> 00:35:06,234
- Where is he?
- Give it a minute.

724
00:35:11,109 --> 00:35:12,980
[Patrick]
'Ah-ha! There he is.'

725
00:35:14,068 --> 00:35:15,722
If anything happens to him..

726
00:35:15,809 --> 00:35:18,768
'Everyone's safe,
so don't worry.'

727
00:35:18,855 --> 00:35:21,684
It's all gonna turn out fine.

728
00:35:28,691 --> 00:35:29,866
Shall we?

729
00:35:41,226 --> 00:35:43,315
- You're the bounty hunter.
- Excuse me?

730
00:35:43,402 --> 00:35:45,273
This is about your bounty.

731
00:35:46,970 --> 00:35:48,363
[under breath]
Oh, man.

732
00:35:54,543 --> 00:35:56,415
Hey, I don't have time.

733
00:35:56,502 --> 00:35:59,200
Listen, I just need you
to take O'Brien to Mexico

734
00:35:59,287 --> 00:36:01,028
and let him loose.

735
00:36:01,115 --> 00:36:03,291
You do that, I'll double
whatever they're paying you.

736
00:36:03,378 --> 00:36:05,424
- What?
- Exactly what I said.

737
00:36:05,511 --> 00:36:08,949
- I'll double your bounty.
- I don't do that.

738
00:36:09,036 --> 00:36:10,777
Fine, I'll triple it.

739
00:36:10,864 --> 00:36:12,779
Why?

740
00:36:12,866 --> 00:36:15,782
Look, it doesn't matter.
Will you do it?

741
00:36:15,869 --> 00:36:20,003
You killed Chief Green
and the druggie, didn't you?

742
00:36:20,090 --> 00:36:21,962
You're worried O'Brien
can identify you.

743
00:36:22,049 --> 00:36:25,226
Just...just name your price.

744
00:36:25,313 --> 00:36:26,575
A million bucks.

745
00:36:26,662 --> 00:36:28,142
- Come on. That's not even..
- Whoa!

746
00:36:28,229 --> 00:36:30,013
Might need your daddy's
checkbook for that.

747
00:36:30,100 --> 00:36:31,798
Why? What's going on?

748
00:36:31,885 --> 00:36:34,279
O'Brien didn't witness anything.
He was nowhere near the cabin.

749
00:36:34,366 --> 00:36:36,933
But you were, weren't you?

750
00:36:37,020 --> 00:36:39,806
No. I..
Why would you say that?

751
00:36:39,893 --> 00:36:42,635
Well, you gave us that
videotape so easily.

752
00:36:42,722 --> 00:36:45,115
Practically handed us
Zubov as a suspect

753
00:36:45,203 --> 00:36:47,248
'and then there's the drugs.'

754
00:36:47,335 --> 00:36:50,947
A little partial to the cocaine,
aren't you, Chad?

755
00:36:53,298 --> 00:36:55,691
- No, I'm not.
- Okay, a lot partial.

756
00:36:55,778 --> 00:36:59,129
Dilated pupils, hyper-alert.
You're burning up.

757
00:36:59,217 --> 00:37:02,263
That's why you have this, uh,
personal air conditioner

758
00:37:02,350 --> 00:37:04,047
in an already-cool room.

759
00:37:04,134 --> 00:37:05,788
'And when I shook your hand'

760
00:37:05,875 --> 00:37:08,051
your pulse was thumping
like a jackhammer, my friend.

761
00:37:08,138 --> 00:37:09,923
Okay. Stay there!

762
00:37:10,010 --> 00:37:11,794
Chad, let him go.

763
00:37:11,881 --> 00:37:13,056
Stay there!

764
00:37:19,585 --> 00:37:22,849
Don't be stupid, Chad.
Let him go.

765
00:37:22,936 --> 00:37:25,460
Stay back, I'll shoot him!
I swear I'll shoot him!

766
00:37:25,547 --> 00:37:26,722
[alarm bell ringing]

767
00:37:26,809 --> 00:37:29,203
[both grunting]

768
00:37:41,084 --> 00:37:43,348
Nicely done, Lisbon family.

769
00:37:45,828 --> 00:37:48,701
[bell continues ringing]

770
00:37:55,185 --> 00:37:57,144
Our attorney
will be here soon.

771
00:37:57,231 --> 00:37:58,145
- What's the point?
- Son--

772
00:37:58,232 --> 00:38:00,930
I just wanna
be done with it.

773
00:38:01,017 --> 00:38:03,019
When did you start
dealing drugs?

774
00:38:03,106 --> 00:38:05,021
A year ago.

775
00:38:07,197 --> 00:38:10,026
Look, he doesn't
pay me anything.

776
00:38:10,113 --> 00:38:11,767
Dealing does.

777
00:38:11,854 --> 00:38:14,683
You were dealing to Steve Kasser
the night of the murders?

778
00:38:16,076 --> 00:38:17,556
What happened next?

779
00:38:17,643 --> 00:38:21,124
[Chad]
'That's when the cop came by.'

780
00:38:21,211 --> 00:38:23,518
She told us to take it easy.

781
00:38:23,605 --> 00:38:26,042
Then she started to talk
to Steve about his mother.

782
00:38:26,129 --> 00:38:29,524
'All I could think about was how
my father was gonna disown me'

783
00:38:29,611 --> 00:38:33,572
'how I'm gonna lose everything.'

784
00:38:33,659 --> 00:38:35,530
'I was so high.'

785
00:38:39,969 --> 00:38:42,972
I put Chief Green
in her trunk.

786
00:38:43,059 --> 00:38:45,279
'I tried to get Steven too'

787
00:38:45,366 --> 00:38:48,282
but he was too heavy,
so I left him there.

788
00:38:48,369 --> 00:38:50,066
Look, I didn't wanna
kill Steve, okay?

789
00:38:50,153 --> 00:38:52,808
I didn't wanna kill anybody,
but I had to.

790
00:38:52,895 --> 00:38:54,810
That has to count
for something, right?

791
00:38:56,377 --> 00:38:57,509
No.

792
00:39:04,080 --> 00:39:05,647
[knocking]

793
00:39:05,734 --> 00:39:07,432
- Hey.
- Hey.

794
00:39:07,519 --> 00:39:09,390
The kid wanted to say good-bye.

795
00:39:10,826 --> 00:39:12,132
[chuckling]

796
00:39:14,961 --> 00:39:16,919
Give me a minute
with your aunt, huh?

797
00:39:17,006 --> 00:39:18,791
- Yeah.
- Love you.

798
00:39:18,878 --> 00:39:20,575
Love you too.

799
00:39:25,363 --> 00:39:28,278
Listen, do you still
want O'Brien?

800
00:39:30,803 --> 00:39:32,848
Well...yeah, sure.

801
00:39:32,935 --> 00:39:34,546
He's downstairs in holding.

802
00:39:34,633 --> 00:39:36,330
I'll have them
release him to you.

803
00:39:36,417 --> 00:39:40,029
Wow. Thanks.

804
00:39:40,116 --> 00:39:42,989
This doesn't mean I think
what you're doing is right

805
00:39:43,076 --> 00:39:46,514
but I don't know.
Maybe I'm wrong.

806
00:39:46,601 --> 00:39:48,386
You got a great kid there

807
00:39:48,473 --> 00:39:50,518
so you're obviously
doing something right.

808
00:39:53,782 --> 00:39:56,306
I'm proud of you, Tommy.

809
00:39:56,394 --> 00:39:58,700
Maybe even a little envious.

810
00:40:03,531 --> 00:40:05,272
Thanks, Rees.

811
00:40:13,585 --> 00:40:16,544
I love you, Tommy.

812
00:40:16,631 --> 00:40:22,289
And, um, you know that
I'm always here for you, right?

813
00:40:22,376 --> 00:40:25,727
Yeah, I know that.

814
00:40:25,814 --> 00:40:27,207
Okay.

815
00:40:35,084 --> 00:40:36,738
[exhaling deeply]

816
00:40:36,825 --> 00:40:38,697
[whispering]
Be careful, Tommy.

817
00:40:47,793 --> 00:40:50,012
[theme music]

